 <giedre.s@8devices.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:47:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: virtual-thermal-zones correct the Kconfig help text.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ref.: 8devices/software/yocto/meta-8dev-qcs405#799

The help text omitted weighted-average from the list of aggregation
methods, described the driver only in general terms, and did not say
that the module has to be loaded explicitly.

Name weighted-average, state that a source may itself be a virtual zone
so zones can be chained, and that cycles and chains deeper than eight
are rejected.  Say why modprobe is required: the driver registers its
own platform device when it initialises, so there is no device present
beforehand for the module to be autoloaded from.

Signed-off-by: Giedrė Šimkūnaitė <giedre.s@8devices.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 53b6f0e7eff0f1898de67ed77c4a5df5c95130d5)
Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 drivers/thermal/Kconfig | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/Kconfig b/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
index a0adcbb00a2b..3aff150a2d18 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
@@ -257,22 +257,24 @@ config VIRTUAL_THERMAL_ZONES
 	  to existing sensors.
 
 	  For multiple-source zones, the driver supports various temperature
-	  aggregation methods including: maximum, minimum, average, median,
-	  rolling average, and exponential average calculations. Default logic
-	  is 'max' for multiple sources.
+	  aggregation methods: maximum, minimum, average, median, weighted
+	  average, rolling average and exponential average. Default logic is
+	  'max' for multiple sources.
 
 	  Virtual thermal zones are configured via device tree nodes with
 	  compatible = "virtual-thermal-zone" and can define their own
 	  trip points and cooling device bindings.
 
-	  This driver can be used on any platform to aggregate sensor
-	  temperatures or create system-wide thermal zones.
+	  A source may itself be a virtual zone, so zones can be chained;
+	  dependency cycles and chains deeper than 8 are rejected.
 
 	  Say Y here if you want to enable virtual thermal zone support.
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
-	  will be called virtual-thermal-zones.
+	  will be called virtual-thermal-zones. It has to be loaded explicitly:
+	  the driver creates its own platform device when it initialises, so
+	  there is no device present beforehand to autoload it from.
 
 config HISI_THERMAL
 	tristate "Hisilicon thermal driver"
